  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "So the filter is not limited to the rows currently loaded \u2014 that part works correctly, and it works across all four tabs and both locations. The problem is only that the list is built one entry per unit number. Also ruled out: it is not the date range (the same six are missing on a narrower range), and it is not the "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "B104",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " case alone \u2014 that one has the additional oddity that its option carries no vehicle identification number even though the work order does."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 2
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "4. Expected behaviour"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Every asset that appears on the report should be offered in the Asset filter, and typing either identifier should find it. The Work In Progress specification, version 9, requires (S7-R4):"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "blockquote",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "paragraph",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "The toolbar has an Asset filter, a searchable type-ahead multi-select listing the assets present across all open jobs in the current scope. Each option shows the unit number and the vehicle identification number, and the user's typed text matches against EITHER the unit number OR the vehicle identification number."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Two vehicles that share a unit number are still two assets present on the report, so both should be listed and both identification numbers should match."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "For non-vehicle assets, note that this field holds the unit's serial number rather than a true vehicle identification number \u2014 that is expected and is not what this ticket is about."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 2
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "5. Current behaviour"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "The Asset filter offers one entry per unit number. Where two vehicles share a unit number only one is listed, the listed entry shows only that one's identification number, and the other vehicle's identification number matches nothing typed into the filter. Six vehicles are affected on the current test data."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 2
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "6. Images"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "No screenshot is attached, and the reason is stated rather than implied: this session could not open the application's screens at all. The application front end would not accept the browser session available to this run, and the one route that produces a signed-in browser could not be used because it would have reset a sign-in shared with two other testers working on other branches at the same time. What is written above was read directly from the data the Asset filter is built from, and the full response is saved with our evidence so the six missing vehicles can be confirmed without repeating the work."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "attrs": {
    "level": 2
   },
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "7. Technical details for developers"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "The option list comes from its own endpoint, separate from the row data:"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "codeBlock",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "GET /api/reporting/reports/work-in-progress/filters\n    ?from=2025-09-01T00:00:00.000Z&to=2026-08-05T23:59:59.000Z\n    &locations=b3c8c820-f815-4cf1-8938-10956c5ee71a,f8a8b802-7780-4b16-bf10-343caeb616b2\n-> HTTP 200\n   {\"data\":{\"advisors\":[15 items],\"customers\":[215 items],\"assets\":[278 items]}}"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Each asset entry has the shape "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"value\":\"854\",\"unit_number\":\"854\",\"vin\":\"5SHFE4730MB001604\"",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "code"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "}, and "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "value",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "code"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": " falls back to the identification number when there is no unit number (106 of the 278 entries are of that kind). Counting the 172 entries that do have a unit number: "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "no unit number appears twice",
     "marks": [
      {
       "type": "strong"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": ", which is the defect \u2014 the list is keyed by unit number rather than by asset."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "content": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Compared against the complete row set fetched as "
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "GET /api/reporting/reports/work-in-progress?...&tab=<each of the four>&pagination[rowsPerPage]=1000",
